32	14	gmail	19e407d3fc5e5b70	inbound	brandscheffer@protonmail.com	info@shortstayinn.com	Re: Return to NL	Hi Sander\n\nThanks for the message and the text. I was looking at some of the options before proceeding. It's always tricky to arrange these things from overseas.\n\nDen Bosch is more convenient for me, but the prices are also higher. I'm thinking that maybe I should look around Enschede for an apartment. From what I can see, I definitely get more for my money than I would in Den Bosch, so I think to start with I will come back to you, and then make a decision when I am there.\n\nI want a room with a kitchen and bathroom and probably prefer to be at the back than the front, that room got seriously hot last year! So, if if you can suggest a couple of options for 2 months that would be great.\n\nI will simply transfer funds to you like last time if that works for you. I arrive back in NL on the 9th of June, but its really early in the morning, so I will stay in a hotel at the airport and then make my way to you on the 10, arriving around 12 midday.\n\nLook forward to hearing from you and coming back to the Short Stay Inn!\n\nBest\n\nBrand\n\nBrand Scheffer\nDirect: +356 7903 4134\n\nSent with [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail/home) secure email.\n\nOn Sunday, May 17th, 2026 at 5:16 AM, Short-Stay Inn <info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\n\n> Hi Brand,\n>\n> Good to hear you are coming back to NL! That sounds like a big move.\n> Just to make sure. 'Den Bosch' area is quite far from Enschede (2 hr by car 3 hr by train).\n> Are you sure you like to stay in Enschede in the beginning?\n>\n> From the 9th of June we have several options available at the moment:\n> - Room 4 in Bilderdijkstraat (approx 300 m from where you stayed last time) ; private double room and bathroom and airconditioning on 2nd floor but kitchen en garden are shared\n> - Room 5, same building and conditions but bigger and on the ground floor.\n> - Studio 4 in same building as you stayed last time; double room at back side of building. Private bathroom and kitchen\n> - Studio 6; same building but single room; also private bathroom and kitchen at the back side of the building.\n>\n> Please let me know if you have a preferance and I will make you a quotation.\n>\n> Look forward to hearing from you!\n>\n> Kind regards,\n> Sander\n>\n> On Fri, 15 May 2026 at 19:43, brandscheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com> wrote:\n>\n>> Hi Sander\n>>\n>> I'm finally heading back to NL! I will be back by the 9th of next month and looking for a place to stay.\n>>\n>> I am actually relocating and will register myself as resident again. Most likely I will look around the Den Bosch area for logistical reasons, but that means for the first couple of months I will need a place to stay.\n>>\n>> If you have any availability do let me know and I'll be happy to see you again!\n>>\n>> Kind regards\n>>\n>> Brand\n>>\n>> Brand Scheffer\n>> Direct: +356 7903 4134\n>>\n>> Sent with [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail/home) secure email.	2026-05-19 13:46:44+00	{"gmail": {"id": "19e407d3fc5e5b70", "threadId": "19e2cbc0e7168660", "labelIds": ["Label_1738314444454715560", "IMPORTANT", "CATEGORY_PERSONAL", "INBOX"], "snippet": "Hi Sander Thanks for the message and the text. I was looking at some of the options before proceeding. It&#39;s always tricky to arrange these things from overseas. Den Bosch is more convenient for me,", "payload": {"partId": "", "mimeType": "multipart/alternative", "filename": "", "headers": [{"name": "Delivered-To", "value": "info@shortstayinn.com"}, {"name": "Received", "value": "by 2002:a05:6a10:6f2c:b0:6d1:e48b:57e7 with SMTP id jd44csp2730136pxb;        Tue, 19 May 2026 06:46:50 -0700 (PDT)"}, {"name": "X-Received", "value": "by 2002:a05:690e:1c07:b0:65e:275d:7e1d with SMTP id 956f58d0204a3-65e275d9116mr17599955d50.19.1779198410476;        Tue, 19 May 2026 06:46:50 -0700 (PDT)"}, {"name": "ARC-Seal", "value": "i=1; a=rsa-sha256; t=1779198410; cv=none;        d=google.com;