37	14	gmail	19e4a7d8c0a2b7a0	outbound	info@shortstayinn.com	brandscheffer@protonmail.com	Re: Return to NL	Hello Brand,\r\n\r\nyes with the 9% VAT it would have been more to the €1800 but this is quite\r\na difference unfortunately.\r\n\r\nI switched the CreditCard option on but I don't know how much the proces is\r\nfully automated. But you can try again.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know if somehting is blocking in the proces. And otherwise we\r\nwill figure out another way. Or even when you are here in the Netherlands.\r\n\r\nKind regards, Sander\r\n\r\nOn Wed, 20 May 2026 at 20:19, brandscheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com>\r\nwrote:\r\n\r\n> Hi Sander\r\n>\r\n> That 21% really makes a difference! I had hoped to keep my monthly cost\r\n> around 1700 / 1800  Still it is what it is.\r\n>\r\n> I think I will set myself the target of having everything sorted within 2\r\n> months.  It becomes expensive otherwise.  If everything goes wrong and I\r\n> can't find anywhere, I assume I can always discuss with you and see what is\r\n> available at the time.\r\n>\r\n> Can I make this first payment by credit card? If not I will make the\r\n> payment via my Bank of America account if that is OK, but cc would be\r\n> helpful.\r\n>\r\n> Thanks\r\n>\r\n> Kind regards\r\n>\r\n> Brand\r\n>\r\n> *Brand Scheffer*\r\n> Direct:  +356 7903 4134\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> Sent with Proton Mail <https://proton.me/mail/home> secure email.\r\n>\r\n> On Wednesday, May 20th, 2026 at 6:32 AM, Short-Stay Inn <\r\n> info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\r\n>\r\n> Hi Brand,\r\n> That is wonderful! Thanks for understanding.\r\n>\r\n> I applied a 10 euro per night discount. The government decided to\r\n> increaset the VAT from 9% to 21% that increased the price a lot.\r\n> Important to know. The start of the new study-year is this year from 17th\r\n> of August. That means that from that day it is extreme busy in Enschede.\r\n> This might have effect on the extension abilities. Probably I should have\r\n> told you this before. I know the question is not easy to answer, but do you\r\n> have maybe a rough indicator for the time that you need to find a permanent\r\n> place?\r\n>\r\n> Please let me know if you would like to continue and confirm the booking.\r\n> See you soon, it would be nice to be there to welcome you on the 10th!\r\n>\r\n> Kind regards, Sander\r\n>\r\n> On Tue, 19 May 2026 at 16:45, brandscheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com>\r\n> wrote:\r\n>\r\n>> Hi Sander\r\n>>\r\n>> No problem about 15:00, I'll sleep a little later in Amsterdam and grab a\r\n>> later train. I'll aim for 15:00.\r\n>>\r\n>> Please also let me know prices and feel free to apply as much discount as\r\n>> you like.\r\n>>\r\n>> Look forward to seeing you on the 10th.\r\n>>\r\n>> Kind regards\r\n>>\r\n>> Brand\r\n>>\r\n>> *Brand Scheffer*\r\n>> Direct: +356 7903 4134\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>> Sent with Proton Mail <https://proton.me/mail/home> secure email.\r\n>>\r\n>> On Tuesday, May 19th, 2026 at 10:40 AM, Short-Stay Inn <\r\n>> info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\r\n>>\r\n>> Hi Brand,\r\n>>\r\n>> Sounds like a good plan to check Enschede first, you are right about the\r\n>> value for money here.\r\n>> Studio 4 seems like the best fit based on your preference: private\r\n>> kitchen and bathroom, and at the back of the building. Because studio 4\r\n>> became also the only fit in the mean time. I got a few bookings last days.\r\n>> So I have blocked it now directly for you to make sure it is available. I\r\n>> have blocked it now till the 10th of August, just as a start.\r\n>>\r\n>> On exactly your day of arrival is also the check out of the previous\r\n>> tennant. We need a cleaning window of approx 2 hours, would it be okay for\r\n>> you if the check in is from 15:00?\r\n>>\r\n>> At this moment I am a little bit in a time rush, I have to pick up the\r\n>> boys from school, is it okay i will send tomorrow the quotation? atleast it\r\n>> is now blocked so not stress.\r\n>> Thanks for understanding!\r\n>>\r\n>> Kind regards, Sander\r\n>>\r\n>> On Tue, 19 May 2026 at 15:46, brandscheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com>\r\n>> wrote:\r\n>>\r\n>>> Hi Sander\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Thanks for the message and the text. I was looking at some of the\r\n>>> options before proceeding. It's always tricky to arrange these things from\r\n>>> overseas.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Den Bosch is more convenient for me, but the prices are also higher. I'm\r\n>>> thinking that maybe I should look around Enschede for an apartment. From\r\n>>> what I can see, I definitely get more for my money than I would in Den\r\n>>> Bosch, so I think to start with I will come back to you, and then make a\r\n>>> decision when I am there.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> I want a room with a kitchen and bathroom and probably prefer to be at\r\n>>> the back than the front, that room got seriously hot last year! So, if if\r\n>>> you can suggest a couple of options for 2 months that would be great.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> I will simply transfer funds to you like last time if that works for\r\n>>> you. I arrive back in NL on the 9th of June, but its really early in the\r\n>>> morning, so I will stay in a hotel at the airport and then make my way to\r\n>>> you on the 10, arriving around 12 midday.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Look forward to hearing from you and coming back to the Short Stay Inn!\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Best\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Brand\r\n>>>\r\n>>> *Brand Scheffer*\r\n>>> Direct: +356 7903 4134\r\n>>>\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Sent with Proton Mail <https://proton.me/mail/home> secure email.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> On Sunday, May 17th, 2026 at 5:16 AM, Short-Stay Inn <\r\n>>> info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Hi Brand,\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Good to hear you are coming back to NL! That sounds like a big move.\r\n>>> Just to make sure. 'Den Bosch' area is quite far from Enschede (2 hr by\r\n>>> car 3 hr by train).\r\n>>> Are you sure you like to stay in Enschede in the beginning?\r\n>>>\r\n>>> From the 9th of June we have several options available at the moment:\r\n>>> - Room 4 in Bilderdijkstraat (approx 300 m from where you stayed last\r\n>>> time) ; private double room and bathroom and airconditioning on 2nd floor\r\n>>> but kitchen en garden are shared\r\n>>> - Room 5, same building and conditions but bigger and on the ground\r\n>>> floor.\r\n>>> - Studio 4 in same building as you stayed last time; double room at back\r\n>>> side of building. Private bathroom and kitchen\r\n>>> - Studio 6; same building but single room; also private bathroom and\r\n>>> kitchen at the back side of the building.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Please let me know if you have a preferance and I will make you a\r\n>>> quotation.\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Look forward to hearing from you!\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Kind regards,\r\n>>> Sander\r\n>>>\r\n>>> On Fri, 15 May 2026 at 19:43, brandscheffer <\r\n>>> brandscheffer@protonmail.com> wrote:\r\n>>>\r\n>>>> Hi Sander\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> I'm finally heading back to NL! I will be back by the 9th of next month\r\n>>>> and looking for a place to stay.\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> I am actually relocating and will register myself as resident again.\r\n>>>> Most likely I will look around the Den Bosch area for logistical reasons,\r\n>>>> but that means for the first couple of months I will need a place to stay.\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> If you have any availability do let me know and I'll be happy to see\r\n>>>> you again!\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Kind regards\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Brand\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> *Brand Scheffer*\r\n>>>> Direct: +356 7903 4134\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Sent with Proton Mail <https://proton.me/mail/home> secure email.\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>\r\n>>>\r\n>>\r\n>\r\n	2026-05-21 12:23:22+00	{"gmail": {"id": "19e4a7d8c0a2b7a0", "threadId": "19e2cbc0e7168660", "labelIds": ["Label_1738314444454715560", "SENT"], "snippet": "Hello Brand, yes with the 9% VAT it would have been more to the \\u20ac1800 but this is quite a difference unfortunately. I switched the CreditCard option on but I don&#39;t know how much the proces is fully", "payload": {"partId": "", "mimeType": "multipart/alternative", "filename": "", "headers": [{"nam