87	33	gmail	196db7248f75e488	inbound	brandscheffer@protonmail.com	info@shortstayinn.com	Re: Short-Stay Inn advert form "[your-subject]"	Hi Sander\n\nFurther to our conversation earlier today (probably yesterday for you) I just wanted to confirm I will accept your proposed studio unit near the train station in the centre of town.\n\nAs discussed my dates are now arrival on the 27th of this month, not sure what tie I land at Schiphol but I'll advise you of that in due course. If you can confirm a mattress toppper to turn the two singles into a double, that will be great.\n\nI will transfer the first tranche to your bank shortly.\n\nLooking forward to meeting you,\n\nKind regards\n\nBrand Scheffer\nDirect: +356 7903 4134\n\nSent with [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail/home) secure email.\n\nOn Thursday, May 15th, 2025 at 8:36 AM, brandscheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com> wrote:\n\n> Dear Sander\n>\n> Thanks for the quick response.\n>\n> Your suggestion sounds good and I am certainly available for a Zoom or Teams call. There is a 9 hour time difference between us, but if we arrange sometime between 7 am and 9 am my time that would be 4pm and 6pm your time that would work.\n>\n> Just let me know when you want to do that and I will make myself available.\n>\n> Kind regards\n>\n> Brand Scheffer\n> Direct: +356 7903 4134\n>\n> Sent with [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail/home) secure email.\n>\n> On Thursday, May 15th, 2025 at 6:41 AM, Short-Stay Inn <info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\n>\n>> Dear Mr. Scheffer,\n>>\n>> Thank you for the additional information. We appreciate you providing a clearer understanding of your requirements. We also noted your preference for English and perhaps your Dutch will improve during your stay in the Netherlands!\n>>\n>> To further discuss your needs or if you have any questions, we would be happy to schedule a video call at your convenience.\n>>\n>> Based on your preferences, I have attached a quotation for a luxurious studio that might be a great fit for you. It enjoys a convenient location near the city center and the central station and features high-speed fiber optic internet with speeds up to 1000 Mbps, as well as a private bathroom and kitchen.\n>>\n>> Please feel free to reach out if you have any questions about this option.\n>>\n>> Kind regards,\n>>\n>> Sander\n>>\n>> Short-Stay Inn\n>> Tromplaan 8, 7511JK EnschedeThe Netherlands\n>>\n>> www.ShortStayInn.com\n>>\n>> Telephone: 0031 (0) 53 8200 946\n>>\n>> On Wed, 14 May 2025 at 18:20, brandscheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com> wrote:\n>>\n>>> Hello\n>>>\n>>> Thanks for your response. I have filled in your calendar, but I didn't see any other questions or information you were looking for. So to recap and give you a better idea, I have provided some more details.\n>>>\n>>> I am a Dutch national, born 1952, but my written Dutch is so bad I write in English. I am currently in the US, (Los Angeles) hence the time lag in replying. I need to be back in NL for 3 months to sort out some personal administrative issues but will continue to work remotely. So internet is essential for me.\n>>>\n>>> On your calendar, I listed 92 days, but I can be flexible. I suggested arrival on 23rd of this month and departure on the 25th of August. I'm happy to move those dates around a little if that makes it easier.\n>>>\n>>> I am looking for a self contained unit where I can stay and work while I sort out my personal affairs. So that means a bed preferably a double, a bathroom and a kitchen. It could be a studio or small apartment.\n>>>\n>>> I hope that's sufficient information for you, but let me know if you need more.\n>>>\n>>> Look forward to hearing from you\n>>>\n>>> Regards\n>>>\n>>> Brand Scheffer\n>>> Direct: +356 7903 4134\n>>>\n>>> Sent with [Proton Mail](https://proton.me/mail/home) secure email.\n>>>\n>>> On Wednesday, May 14th, 2025 at 1:29 AM, Short-Stay Inn <info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\n>>>\n>>>> Dear Mr. Scheffer,\n>>>>\n>>>> Thank you for your inquiry. We also received your request regarding the Atjehstraat location. Unfortunately, that apartment is currently occupied.\n>>>>\n>>>> However, we do have 4 other locations available during the dates you requested.\n>>>>\n>>>> To help us find the most suitable option for you, could you please fill out this form: [https://beds24.com/book-guestfillout]? This will allow us to better understand your specific requirements.\n>>>>\n>>>> Kind regards,\n>>>>\n>>>> Sander Lock\n>>>>\n>>>> Short-Stay Inn\n>>>> Tromplaan 8, 7511JK EnschedeThe Netherlands\n>>>>\n>>>> www.ShortStayInn.com\n>>>>\n>>>> Telephone: 0031 (0) 53 8200 946\n>>>>\n>>>> On Tue, 13 May 2025 at 20:53, <info@shortstayinn.com> wrote:\n>>>>\n>>>>> Hi Short-Stay Inn,\n>>>>>\n>>>>> Someone just contacted you via Short-Stay Inn!\n>>>>> You can find the details below.\n>>>>>\n>>>>> From: Brand Scheffer <brandscheffer@protonmail.com>\n>>>>> Contact for [Bilderdijkstraat A (studio 5) (Minimum stay = 1 week)](https://shortstayinn.com/rental/bilderdijkstraat-studio-5-minimaal-verblijf-1-week/)\n>>>>>\n>>>>> Message:\n>>>>> 21st May for 3 months one person occupancy\n>>>>>\n>>>>> --\n>>>>> This e-mail was sent from a [Bilderdijkstraat A (studio 5) (Minimum stay = 1 week)](https://shortstayinn.com/rental/bilderdijkstraat-studio-5-minimaal-verblijf-1-week/).\n>>>>> Replying to this e-mail, will automatically reply to the customer (brandscheffer@protonmail.com).	2025-05-16 23:33:37+00	{"gmail": {"id": "196db7248f75e488", "threadId": "196cafe74bfd2a52", "labelIds": ["IMPORTANT", "Label_4139206071984797100", "CATEGORY_PERSONAL"], "snippet": "Hi Sander Further to our conversation earlier today (probably yesterday for you) I just wanted to confirm I will accept your proposed studio unit near the train station in the centre of town. As", "payload": {"partId": "", "mimeType": "multipart/alternative", "filename": "", "headers": [{"name": "Delivered-To", "value": "info@shortstayinn.com"}, {"name": "Received", "value": "by 2002