157	78	gmail	1993cf067761373a	outbound	info@shortstayinn.com	kalsharajapaksa@gmail.com	Re: address investigation	Good morning Kalsha,\r\n\r\nI just received an email from municipality that they have stopped the\r\nprocess and that everything went back to normal.\r\nMaybe you will receive another mail about it, this was not mentioned in\r\ntheir reply, but if you do, please let me know.\r\n\r\nSo it seems all solved ;-)\r\n\r\nSince a few months Johanna is not involved with the Short-Stay company\r\nanymore, me and Alberto took it all over in the communication and\r\narrangements.\r\nWith Alberto I agreed that he became the first in line contact with all the\r\ntechnical matters of all the locations and I will be the contact person for\r\nall the administration related matters.\r\n\r\nBecause we are neighbours I would like you to also have my private phone\r\nnumber so you can always call in urgent matters. You already have Johanna's\r\nprivate phone number and you can also contact Johanna, but basically she\r\nwill forward all Short-Stay topics to me.\r\nMy private mobile is: 0031641765017\r\n\r\n\r\nKind regards, Sander\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nShort-Stay Inn\r\nTromplaan 8, 7511JK Enschede\r\nThe Netherlands\r\n\r\nwww.ShortStayInn.com\r\n\r\nTelephone: 0031 (0) 53 8200 946\r\n\r\n\r\nOn Thu, 11 Sept 2025 at 19:23, Kalsha Rajapaksa <kalsharajapaksa@gmail.com>\r\nwrote:\r\n\r\n> Hi sanders,\r\n> Thank you for the update and assistance\r\n>\r\n> Kind regards\r\n> Kalsha\r\n>\r\n> On Thu, 11 Sep 2025 at 18:11, Short-Stay Inn <info@shortstayinn.com>\r\n> wrote:\r\n>\r\n>> Hi Kalsha,\r\n>> I have send an email to the municipality to confirm that you are still\r\n>> living on the adres of Bilderdijkstraat and asked them if my email is\r\n>> sufficient for them that we don't need to take any other actions.\r\n>>\r\n>> Let's wait and see what they say.\r\n>>\r\n>> Kind regards, Sander\r\n>>\r\n>> Short-Stay Inn\r\n>> Tromplaan 8, 7511JK Enschede\r\n>> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/Tromplaan+8,+7511JK+Enschede+The+Netherlands?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>> The Netherlands\r\n>> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/Tromplaan+8,+7511JK+Enschede+The+Netherlands?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>>\r\n>> www.ShortStayInn.com\r\n>>\r\n>> Telephone: 0031 (0) 53 8200 946\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>> On Thu, 11 Sept 2025 at 14:25, Kalsha Rajapaksa <\r\n>> kalsharajapaksa@gmail.com> wrote:\r\n>>\r\n>>> Hi sander,\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Thank you for letting me know\r\n>>>\r\n>>> Kind regards\r\n>>> Kalsha\r\n>>>\r\n>>> On Thu, 11 Sep 2025 at 14:22, Short-Stay Inn <info@shortstayinn.com>\r\n>>> wrote:\r\n>>>\r\n>>>> Hi Kalsha,\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Once in a while the municipality is doing these researches on\r\n>>>> addresses. Another person just registered at the same location I suppose\r\n>>>> that this has triggered the municipality to send these standard emails.\r\n>>>> I will contact them and ask about it.\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Let me come back to you if I hear more about it.\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Kind regards, Sander\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Short-Stay Inn\r\n>>>> Tromplaan 8, 7511JK Enschede\r\n>>>> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/Tromplaan+8,+7511JK+Enschede+The+Netherlands?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>>>> The Netherlands\r\n>>>> <https://www.google.com/maps/search/Tromplaan+8,+7511JK+Enschede+The+Netherlands?entry=gmail&source=g>\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> www.ShortStayInn.com\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> Telephone: 0031 (0) 53 8200 946\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>> On Thu, 11 Sept 2025 at 11:34, Kalsha Rajapaksa <\r\n>>>> kalsharajapaksa@gmail.com> wrote:\r\n>>>>\r\n>>>>> Hi,\r\n>>>>> Please find the forwarded the email I received\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> Thank you\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> Kind regards\r\n>>>>> Kalsha\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> ---------- Forwarded message ---------\r\n>>>>> From: <burgerzaken1@enschede.nl>\r\n>>>>> Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2025 at 09:47\r\n>>>>> Subject: address investigation\r\n>>>>> To: <kalsharajapaksa@gmail.com>\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> Subject: Register change of address / pending removal from BRP.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> Dear Kalsha Rajapaksa,\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> According to our information, you are no longer residing at the\r\n>>>>> address that you are currently registered at. We have not yet received a\r\n>>>>> declaration of relocation from you.\r\n>>>>> That is why we have started an investigation and are trying to find\r\n>>>>> your new home address.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> *What we expect from you*\r\n>>>>> Report your move within 5 working days.\r\n>>>>> Do you live in Enschede?\r\n>>>>> With your DigiD you log in to our website enschede.nl/verhuizen to\r\n>>>>> report your move.\r\n>>>>> Would you prefer to register your move in person? Call our 5-digit\r\n>>>>> telephone number 14 053 to schedule an appointment between 9:00 am and 5:00\r\n>>>>> pm.\r\n>>>>> When contacting us from abroad, call +31 53 481 81 81.\r\n>>>>> If you live in another municipality within the Netherlands, please\r\n>>>>> contact your new municipality.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> *What is going to happen now?*\r\n>>>>> If we do not receive a declaration of your move within 5 working days,\r\n>>>>> we will conduct an additional investigation. If we do not find a new home\r\n>>>>> address during the additional investigation and if you do not provide us\r\n>>>>> with your correct address within 4 weeks of receiving this e-mail, we can\r\n>>>>> impose an administrative fine of up to € 325.00 (Article 4.17 of the BRP\r\n>>>>> Act).\r\n>>>>> More information on the administrative fine can be found at\r\n>>>>> enschede.nl/bestuurlijkeboete.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> We also record in the BRP that you have move abroad from the date of\r\n>>>>> this email (Article 2.22 of the BRP Act). This means that you will no\r\n>>>>> longer be registered in the BRP as of that moment (Article 2.43 of the BRP\r\n>>>>> Act).\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> The most important consequences of moving abroad are listed below:\r\n>>>>> -           If you receive social assistance benefits, these will stop.\r\n>>>>> -           Your health insurance will end.\r\n>>>>> -           You will no longer receive benefits from the\r\n>>>>> Belastingdienst.\r\n>>>>> -           You may be required to reimburse benefits or social\r\n>>>>> assistance you have received.\r\n>>>>> -           You cannot apply for a new personal identification card or\r\n>>>>> driver’s licence.\r\n>>>>> -           You cannot submit a tax return.\r\n>>>>> -           The new resident of your former address cannot request\r\n>>>>> subsidies or benefits.\r\n>>>>> -           The new resident may request that you pay for these costs.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> *How to prevent receiving a fine*\r\n>>>>> If you provide your correct address within 4 weeks of the date of this\r\n>>>>> email, you will comply with the BRP Act. You will not receive a fine.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> If you wish to respond to this email, I advise you to do this within 4\r\n>>>>> weeks of the date recorded on this email\r\n>>>>> There are several ways for you to respond:\r\n>>>>> -           A written response. You may use the return envelope.\r\n>>>>> -           Via email. Our email address is adresonderzoek@enschede.nl\r\n>>>>> .\r\n>>>>> -           You can also provide a verbal response. Call our 5-digit\r\n>>>>> telephone number 14 053 to schedule an appointment. When contacting us from\r\n>>>>> abroad, call +31 53 481 81 81. We are available from Monday to Friday\r\n>>>>> between 9:00 am and 5:00 pm.\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> Sincerely,\r\n>>>>> On behalf of the Mayor and Aldermen,\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>> Enforcement/Address Investigation Team\r\n>>>>> Service Department\r\n>>>>>\r\n>>>>\r\n	2025-09-12 08:00:11+00	{"gmail": {"id": "1993cf067761373a", "threadId": "199382070482ebe4", "labelIds": ["SENT"], "snippet": "Good morning Kalsha, I just received an email from municipality that they have stopped the process and that everything went back to normal. Maybe you will receive another mail about it, this was not", "payload": {"partId": "", "mimeType": "multipart/alternative", "filename": "", "headers"